# The build context is `backend/`, so these are relative to it.
#
# Two of these entries are load-bearing rather than housekeeping:
#
#   .env      — the image is a build artifact that gets pushed to a registry.
#               Baking real Supabase, Clerk, and Stripe credentials into a layer
#               puts them somewhere `docker history` can read them back out, and
#               deleting the file in a later layer does not remove it from the
#               earlier one. Config arrives as environment variables at runtime.
#   .venv/    — a Windows virtualenv full of win32 wheels, which would both
#               balloon the image and shadow the Linux packages pip just
#               installed if it landed on top of them.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tests run in CI against the source tree, not in the image. Leaving them out
# keeps the runtime surface to what actually serves traffic.
tests/
.pytest_cache/
pytest.ini

# The local dev launcher — its only job is the Windows event-loop policy, and
# the container starts uvicorn through docker-entrypoint.sh instead.
run.py

README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
